Answer with either {"tool": "<name>", "args": {...}, "why": "<one clause>"} or {"stop": true}.
An action naming a tool that is not listed, arguments the schema does not allow, or a path outside
the package will be refused and recorded as refused.

Answer with one JSON object and nothing else: no prose before or after it, no explanation, no markdown fence. It must validate against this JSON schema:
{"additionalProperties": false, "description": "One action of the bounded loop, exactly as spec section 3.12 writes it.\n\nAttributes:\n    tool: The tool to call, or ``None`` when stopping.\n    args: Its arguments.\n    why: Why this call is worth making.\n    stop: ``True`` to end the loop.", "properties": {"tool": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "title": "Tool"}, "args": {"additionalProperties": true, "title": "Args", "type": "object"}, "why": {"default": "", "title": "Why", "type": "string"}, "stop": {"default": false, "title": "Stop", "type": "boolean"}}, "title": "FollowUpAction", "type": "object"}
